{
    "background_story": "Jocelyn was a free-spirited artist known for bringing levity to those around her. Her paintings were vibrant and playful, reflecting her infectious optimism. As a children's hospital art therapist, Jocelyn used her talents to lift the spirits of young patients. She'd wheel her cart of colorful supplies into the rooms, and with a twinkle in her eye, coax even the most reluctant kids into creating masterpieces. Jocelyn's own life hadn't been without challenges, but she'd learned to find the humor in adversity. Her motto, 'Laughter is the best brushstroke,' inspired her students to see the world in a brighter light. With Jocelyn around, the hospital corridors were filled with giggles, and the atmosphere was always a little lighter.",
